VALUES (595, '1c', $t$ASK 595 follow-on: the remaining cuts made whole (a DROPPED question-round reply, the reversed close quotations shown to the judges and in the send-back, and the MEANS block reader)$t$,
  $t$No one's words are cut at the four places W1's read and W4's scan found beside the ASK 595 cut: a DROPPED question-round reply stored cut to 2,000 characters; the reversed close sentences shown to the judges cut to 500; the same sentences quoted in the E-REVCLOSE send-back cut to 400; and the MEANS block the pkgMLS check reads cut to 1,500. (W1's rulings, Wall 11456 items 1 to 3, "same class as 587 A"; W4's notes595c.md; the library line 2277 reader was added on the coordinator's order, as notes595c.md gives it.)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write it" at 07:57 CST 2026-11-24, with no engine or child run live (Wall 11513; audit 41371). Engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN 04273989 to 1afd3099-bcaf-42e5-bace-f4aae59b2b37; child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT c9acb53a to 18570075-f207-4933-b32d-346e40668995. LIB 04ac120b9bf3a19c, MAP e12df49c7db048c0. What changed, each change only the removal of a .slice(0,N) (W1's character walk, Wall 11490): (1) QR Final stores a DROPPED question's first_reply and second_reply whole (2 cuts of 2,000); (2) QR Follow Final stores a DROPPED continuation's reply whole (1 cut of 2,000); (3) Panel Build and Build Independent Verdict show the close quotation and the earlier quotation of the ASK 590 reversed-close blocks whole, verse form and link form (4 cuts of 500 in each node; Build Independent Verdict does not run and changes only so the twins stay equal); (4) Shared Library line 3564, engine and child: the E-REVCLOSE send-back quotes both sentences whole (2 cuts of 400); (5) Shared Library line 2277, engine and child: mlsBlock returns the debater's MEANS block whole (1 cut of 1,500). 13 engine cuts and 3 child cuts removed, none added (Wall 11490). The database function odv1_record_question_round cuts nothing and the log has no length-limited column (Wall 11490). W1's R1 (Wall 11490): mlsBlock feeds mlsCarried in the pkgMLS check (K-ML, TRIAL, list only), so a result can differ. W4's measure (Wall 11493; out_r1_mls.txt): on run 37203 no block over 1,500 characters holds an [L2] or [L3] after the cut, so no result can differ; on 41822, 9 such blocks; on 42071, 11. In those a word can be found carried that was not, so a listed TRIAL item can disappear and none can be added; a missing verse row can add a NOT CHECKED note. The exact replay of the check was NOT RUN (it needs each run's verse rows); the figures are a bound. The check moves no count and removes no seat. W3 found no Wall post in which W1 checks the R1 answer of Wall 11493 before the write; W1 states this when it grades this row. The path: the ASK 595 press "Write 595, then the other three" at 01:58 CST (Wall 11483, 11487); build rev 0 (Wall 11487); W1 PASS with R1 (Wall 11490); R1 answer and card (Wall 11493); the press "Write it" 07:57 CST; the write (Wall 11513); W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11514). IN PART, because no run has executed on 1afd3099 (debate_results last row 21:57 CST 2026-11-23, run 42071): each change is shown by tcuts beside a live control and by the readback, not by a run. NOT IN THIS WRITE: the older TRIAL reversed-close block in Panel Build and Build Independent Verdict (r.close_q, r.earlier_q cut to 400): W1 ruled it dead code that ASK 598 stage A removes (Wall 11490). The other .slice(0,1500) sites and the cut setters named in the standing set's baseline are ASK 597's subject. Consequence for the manual: the ASK 590 entry in part 09.2 was written after this write with each quoted sentence "whole" (version 295, Wall 11519).$t$,
  '11456, 11487, 11490, 11493, 11513, 11514',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), (SELECT id FROM ask_aar_snapshots WHERE ask=595 AND rev='1'),
  to_jsonb($t$His press at 01:58 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread: "Write 595, then the other three" (as Wall 11483 and 11487 give it). His press at 07:57 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread: "Write it" (as Wall 11513 and audit 41371 give it).$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "source": "Wall 11513; audit 41371 (card cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58REvuTCKP2tCi3N7pmN1kpz)", "thread": "W4", "press_time": "07:57 CST 2026-11-24", "question": "not in the record W3 read (the card is in W4's thread); the card text is ask595/w4/cuts/card595c.md 48aa5a92"}$j$::jsonb,
  'W4',
  $j${"md5": "23de946f", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/notes595c.md", "commit": "618f6aa0 (the build files; the write files' commit is not stated in the Wall posts W3 read)", "note": "build notes rev 0; no separate plan: the four cuts were listed with ASK 595 (Wall 11453, 11456)", "source": "md5sum by W3; git log by W3; Wall 11487"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"md5": "bbf4b8d5", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/target_engine_cuts.json", "note": "the engine target on live 04273989; graded, written and read back", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11490, 11514"}, {"md5": "9aff19ee", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/target_child_cuts.json", "note": "the child target on live c9acb53a", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11490, 11514"}, {"md5": "23de946f", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/notes595c.md", "note": "build notes rev 0", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "cb2166ec", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/buildcuts.cjs", "note": "the build script", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "faec5a93", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/tcuts.cjs", "note": "the test, 20 cases", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "63486deb", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/out_tcuts.txt", "note": "test output; the same md5 as write/tcuts_at_write.txt", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "30078d35", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/r1_mls.cjs", "note": "the measure for W1's R1", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "b4ada2de", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/out_r1_mls.txt", "note": "its output", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "48aa5a92", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/card595c.md", "note": "the card text", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "c46bd5cf", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/write/fetchback_eng595c.json", "note": "fetch-back after the write", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "ee637892", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/write/fetchback_child595c.json", "note": "fetch-back after the write, child", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "9609d9c7", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/write/write595c.sh", "note": "the write script; it refuses while any engine or child execution is running", "source": "md5sum by W3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"copy": "restore the engine and the child together from ask595/w4/cuts/write/revert_eng595c.json c68c2119 and revert_child595c.json a94031d5 (to 04273989 and c9acb53a). A revert restores the five cuts.", "path": "ask595/w4/cuts/write/revert_eng595c.json; ask595/w4/cuts/write/revert_child595c.json", "source": "audit 41371; Wall 11513; md5sum by W3"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS with R1 (build rev 0: base equals live, 0 differences; a character walk shows each change only deletes a .slice(0,N); tcuts 20 PASS rerun by W1 on the live base; connections equal)", "wall_id": 11490, "md5_graded": "bbf4b8d5", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11490; the md5 is md5sum by W3 on ask595/w4/cuts/target_engine_cuts.json; W1's post does not print it"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS with R1 (the child target, the same grade: Shared Library only)", "wall_id": 11490, "md5_graded": "9aff19ee", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11490; md5sum by W3 on ask595/w4/cuts/target_child_cuts.json"}]$j$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['bbf4b8d5','9aff19ee'], '[41371]'::jsonb,
  $j$[{"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "ORACLE_DEBATE_V1 moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN", "before": "04273989, 422 nodes", "after": "1afd3099-bcaf-42e5-bace-f4aae59b2b37, 422 nodes"}, {"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT", "before": "c9acb53a, 156 nodes", "after": "18570075-f207-4933-b32d-346e40668995, 156 nodes"}, {"kind": "node", "name": "QR Final", "before": "String(c.first_text==null?'(none)':c.first_text).slice(0,2000); String(second).slice(0,2000)", "after": "the same without .slice(0,2000)"}, {"kind": "node", "name": "QR Follow Final", "before": "String(t==null?'(none)':t).slice(0,2000)", "after": "String(t==null?'(none)':t)"}, {"kind": "node", "name": "Panel Build; Build Independent Verdict", "before": "String(x.closing_q).slice(0,500) and String(x.earlier_q).slice(0,500), twice each in each node", "after": "String(x.closing_q) and String(x.earlier_q)"}, {"kind": "library line", "name": "Shared Library line 3564, engine and child", "before": "String(__x.closing_q).slice(0,400); String(__x.earlier_q).slice(0,400)", "after": "String(__x.closing_q); String(__x.earlier_q)"}, {"kind": "library line", "name": "Shared Library line 2277 (mlsBlock), engine and child", "before": "return out.join('\\n').slice(0,1500);", "after": "return out.join('\\n');"}, {"kind": "library", "name": "Shared Library, engine and child", "before": "LIB 3e42df7e04db6ad2, MAP 97ab265d3c9de960", "after": "LIB 04ac120b9bf3a19c, MAP e12df49c7db048c0"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"name": "tcuts.cjs, 20 cases", "result": "20 PASS at the build, at W1's rerun and at the write: only the five nodes and library lines 2277 and 3564 change; a 3,200-character DROPPED reply is stored whole (first, second, continuation); 900- and 700-character quotations are shown whole in both reversed-close blocks of each twin; the send-back shows 661- and 529-character quotations whole; mlsBlock returns a 2,491-character block whole; each beside a live control that cuts", "source": "Wall 11487 item 3; 11490; 11513; out_tcuts.txt"}, {"name": "Library Check pair", "result": "PASSES: LIB 04ac120b9bf3a19c, MAP e12df49c7db048c0", "source": "Wall 11487; 11513; 11514"}, {"name": "Standing set (ASK 596 core)", "result": "29 PASS, 0 FAIL on the target before the PUT and on live at the readback", "source": "Wall 11513; 11514"}, {"name": "r1_mls.cjs, the bound for W1's R1", "result": "blocks over 1,500 with an [L2] or [L3] after the cut: 37203 none; 41822 9; 42071 11. The exact replay of the check was not run", "source": "Wall 11493; out_r1_mls.txt"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "wall_id": 11514, "result": "MATCH (own fetch: engine 1afd3099, child 18570075; live against the targets 422 of 422 and 156 of 156 nodes, 0 differences; from the base 5 engine nodes and the child's Shared Library only; Library Check PASS; standing set 29 PASS)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"case": "UNEXERCISED. No run has executed on 1afd3099 (debate_results last row 21:57 CST 2026-11-23). EXPECT on the first run: a DROPPED question or continuation row in odv1_question_round_log holds the judge's reply whole; a reversed close sentence over 500 characters stands whole in the judges' prompt and, over 400, in the E-REVCLOSE send-back; a K-ML item is not raised where the carrying [L2] or [L3] stands past character 1,500 of the MEANS block.", "source": "Wall 11513, 11514; SQL by W3; the EXPECT is W3's reading"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"op_doc": "none", "engine_manual": "part 09.2 version 295 (bd64e6b0) already states the reversed close quotations whole (Wall 11519). W3's entries for the DROPPED reply (part 14.0) and the MEANS block (part 09.0) are manual1123/w3/a595c/em_pairs_595c_draft1.json d78a0876, not graded and not carded at the draft of this row"}$j$::jsonb,
